Fix munmap() of the wrong pointer in the dmabuf format table.

linux_dmabuf_format_table() unmapped info->dmabuf_formats -- a small g_new0()
heap struct -- instead of info->dmabuf_format_table, the mmap()ed table it is
actually replacing. The stale pointer was left in place, so the next
zwp_linux_dmabuf_feedback_v1.done event dereferenced unmapped memory in
dmabuf_formats_free() and the process died with SIGSEGV/SEGV_MAPERR.

Reaching it needs a second dmabuf feedback round, which compositors send when
the output or scanout device set changes -- e.g. a monitor hotplug storm.

Fixed upstream in GTK 4.23.3:
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/merge_requests/10166

Local patch against 1:4.22.4-1. Retire this once Arch ships gtk4 >= 4.23.3.

--- a/gdk/wayland/gdkdmabuf-wayland.c
+++ b/gdk/wayland/gdkdmabuf-wayland.c
@@ -117,8 +117,8 @@
 {
   DmabufFormatsInfo *info = data;

-  if (info->dmabuf_formats)
-    munmap (info->dmabuf_formats, sizeof (DmabufFormat) * info->n_dmabuf_formats);
+  if (info->dmabuf_format_table)
+    munmap (info->dmabuf_format_table, sizeof (DmabufFormat) * info->n_dmabuf_formats);

   info->n_dmabuf_formats = size / 16;
   info->dmabuf_format_table = mmap (NULL, size, PROT_READ, MAP_PRIVATE, fd, 0);
